WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.550
A good tiering rule makes its boundaries explicit In
the source rule

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:09.112
NULL is handled first as Unknown Amounts of ten
thousand or more

00:00:09.138 --> 00:00:13.875
are High-Value Amounts of five thousand or more but
below ten thousand

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.588
are Standard Remaining known amounts are Low-Value
Because the thresholds are

00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:23.912
written from high to low each amount reaches the
intended branch An

00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:27.938
exact ten thousand belongs to High-Value and an
exact five thousand belongs

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:32.450
to Standard Later practice adds a separate No Charge
category for an

00:00:32.462 --> 00:00:37.888
exact zero When you design tiers test NULL zero
exact thresholds and

00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:40.000
values just above and below each boundary
